  "title": "Knots are patterns constrained as a whole and free in every part",
  "subject": "The canonical knot test and the 2-CNF/3-CNF boundary",
  "conclusion": "Read on allowed states with erasure as forgetting, a knot is a relation constrained as a whole and free in every part: two loops and a contact have exactly 34, from the single clause ¬A ∨ ¬B ∨ c to parity, which hides one full bit. No 2-CNF with witnesses defines a knot, while three-literal clauses with named intermediates define every knot.",
